87:## Board column
88-
89-One of the four groupings a board places a live issue in: Ready, Blocked, In progress, or Closed. A column is derived, never stored: an `open` issue sits in Ready or Blocked by its readiness, an `in_progress` issue sits in In progress whether or not it is blocked, and a `closed` issue sits in Closed. Because Ready and Blocked are properties rather than statuses, an issue cannot be put into either; it arrives there by being open.
90-
91-## Related dependency
92-
93-A non-blocking association between two issues. `A related B` is undirected to a reader even though its replicated record has `from` and `to` fields: A and B each read the other under `Related`, and neither end implies origin or precedence.
94-
95-## Discovered-from dependency
96-
97-A directed provenance relation between two issues. `A discovered-from B` means A was discovered or derived from B: A reads B under `Discovered from`, while B reads A under `Discovered`.
98-
